<p id="A3.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint contraction, its spectrum lies in
<math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The scalar inequality corresponding to
(<a href="#A3.E7" title="Equation C.7 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>) is</span></p>